.Dd October 31, 2026
.Dt APREFD 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm aprefd
.Nd collect boot-time file reads and update the boot profile
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl dn
.Op Fl k Ar keep
.Op Fl m Ar min
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
reads the access entries that
.Xr aprefetch 4
records during the boot, until the boot recording window closes at the
first login or on timeout.
It then saves them as a trace,
.Pa /var/db/aprefetch/boot.trace ,
renaming the older traces to
.Pa boot.trace.1 ,
.Pa boot.trace.2
and so on, and rebuilds the boot profile
.Pa /etc/aprefetch/boot.prof
from the newest traces, and exits.
.Pp
The profile keeps the pages that were read in at least
.Ar min
of the newest
.Ar keep
traces, or in all of them while there are fewer, so that work done in only
one boot does not make the profile grow.
The pages are grouped into ranges of a file and ordered by the time at
which the newest trace that has them read them first, so that when the
budget of the replay runs out, what was read early is kept.
The profile is limited to 16 MB and to the eight file systems with the most
pages.
.Pp
Both files are written to a temporary name and renamed into place, with
mode 0600.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl d
Stay in the foreground and report to the standard error instead of
.Xr syslog 3 .
.It Fl k Ar keep
Keep and use this many traces, from 1 to 9; 3 by default.
.It Fl m Ar min
A page must be in this many traces; 2 by default.
.It Fl n
Save the trace but leave the profile alone.
With no profile, this records without prefetching.
.El
.Pp
.Nm
is started at boot by
.Pa /etc/rc.d/aprefd
when
.Va aprefd
is set in
.Xr rc.conf 5 ,
which is the default.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /var/db/aprefetch/boot.trace -compact
.It Pa /dev/aprefetch
.It Pa /etc/aprefetch/boot.prof
.It Pa /var/db/aprefetch/boot.trace
.It Pa /var/run/aprefd.pid
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
To measure a boot that records but does not prefetch, remove the profile
and keep
.Nm
from making a new one:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# aprefctl delete boot
# echo 'aprefd_flags="-n"' >> /etc/rc.conf
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr aprefetch 4 ,
.Xr aprefctl 8
.Sh HISTORY
.Nm
was written for AutumnBSD.
